<title>CHINA: China customs says no new tariff on Thai rice.</title>
<headline>China customs says no new tariff on Thai rice.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chinese customs officials said on Monday that import tariffs on processed rice remained unchanged and denied market rumours that a new 13 percent import duty would be levied on Thai fragrant rice.</p>
<p>Officials contacted in Beijing, Tianjin, Shanghai and Guangzhou said China's processed rice import tariffs remained at one percent for rice imported within quotas and 114 percent for that imported outside tariffs.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not heard of any new tariffs,&quot; one customs official said by telephone.</p>
<p>The Thai rice market was roiled last week by rumors that China, a major customer, planned to slap a new 13 tariff on Thai fragrant rice.</p>
<p>China imported 631,180 tonnes of Thai rice in 1996, including some 465,092 tonnes of fragrant rice.</p>
</text>
